# Shell scripts are executed via their shebang; a CRLF would make the kernel look
# for "bash\r" and the hook would silently fail to run on Windows checkouts. That
# failure mode is especially bad here: a WorktreeCreate hook that cannot execute
# costs the user their session. Pin them (and the other text payloads) to LF
# regardless of the user's autocrlf.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch line endings.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
